# La stanza di Lethe: cosa dicono le cose (vedi il vault, "La stanza di Lethe").
# Ogni cue ha il nome del tile dell'oggetto (room_layout.gd): un oggetto con un cue qui
# diventa interagibile da solo. "Lethe:" = i suoi pensieri (col ritratto), il resto è
# il narratore. Stato: truth / lies (GameState), seen("id") = quante volte ci ha già parlato.
# Le righe che non vanno (text_effects.gd): [glitch]...[/glitch] le lettere si guastano,
# [shiver]...[/shiver] tremano, [flicker]...[/flicker] si spengono; [#wrong] in fondo a una
# riga la guasta tutta (e il riquadro sobbalza). Le bugie si guastano.

~ covered_mirror
if seen("covered_mirror") == 0
	A mirror, under a bedsheet. One corner of the glass is uncovered.
	- Look into the corner.
		A sliver of an eye looks back. [shiver]Tired. Red.[/shiver]
		Lethe: ...That's me.
		set truth += 1
	- It's just old furniture.
		Lethe: Just old furniture. Nothing to see here. [#wrong]
		set lies += 1
else
	The sheet hasn't moved. The corner is still there.
=> END

~ wall_calendar
Days crossed out, one by one, up to a circled day.
After that, [glitch]nothing[/glitch].
Lethe: I stopped counting.
=> END

~ food_tray
if seen("food_tray") == 0
	A tray by the door. The food is cold. Untouched.
	There's a note under the cup, with a little heart in the corner.
	- Read the note.
		"Please eat something. I'm not angry. I'll be right outside."
		Lethe: ...
	- Leave it.
		Lethe: Later.
else
	The food is still there. So is the note.
=> END

# Quando bussano (world/door_knock.gd): knocking = c'è qualcuno, knock_over = è già
# successo, answer() = chi bussava se ne va.
~ door
if knocking
	Someone is knocking. A thin line of light under the door, and the shadow of two feet.
	Voice: Lethe? ...Are you awake?
	- I'm awake.
		Lethe: ...I'm awake.
		Voice: Okay. Okay.
		Voice: There's dinner on the tray. Please eat something.
		set truth += 1
	- I'm asleep.
		Lethe: I'm asleep. [#wrong]
		Voice: ...Okay. Goodnight, then.
		set lies += 1
	- Say nothing.
		Lethe: ...
		The voice doesn't ask again.
	do answer()
	Footsteps, going away.
elif knock_over
	The light under the door is gone.
	Lethe: [flicker]They'll come back tomorrow.[/flicker] They always do.
else
	The door. Locked [shiver]from the inside[/shiver].
	Lethe: Not yet.
=> END

~ nightstand
A photo frame, face down.
Lethe: Leave it like that.
=> END

~ paper_balls
Crumpled pages. Every one starts the same way: "[flicker]I'm sorry for[/flicker]"
Lethe: For what? I never get past that line.
=> END

~ dead_plant
A plant nobody has watered in months.
Lethe: It was green, once. [flicker]Wasn't it?[/flicker]
=> END

~ window
The moon, between the curtains.
Lethe: Out there, everything keeps going.
=> END

~ wall_poster
A poster of a magical girl. Her favourite, once.
Lethe: She never ran away from anything.
=> END

~ console
The console is still warm.
Lethe: One more game. Then I'll sleep. [#wrong]
She says that every night.
=> END

~ cushion
A cushion, pressed flat. Someone has sat here for a long time.
=> END

~ desk_pc
The screen glows. Unread messages pile up in a corner.
Lethe: I'll answer [glitch]tomorrow[/glitch].
=> END

~ bed
The bed is unmade.
Lethe: I'm not tired. [#wrong]
=> END

~ shelf
Little heroines on the shelf, all facing the room.
Lethe: Stop looking at me like that.
=> END

~ clothes
A jacket, thrown on the floor. It hasn't been outside in a long time.
=> END

~ trash_bag
A trash bag, tied shut. Nobody takes it out.
=> END
